---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  ComboboxBasics,
  ComboboxGroups,
  ComboboxInputOptions,
  ComboboxMultiple,
  ComboboxPlayground,
  ComboboxStates,
  ComboboxTriggerPicker,
} from '../../components/ComboboxDemo';
---

<Docs title="Combobox" description="Search a list and pick one or more values, in forms and filters.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Combobox</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A text field that filters a list as you type. Pick one value, or many as chips. Use it when a list is too long to
    scan, such as teammates, channels, or time zones. For a short fixed list, use Select.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="combobox-demo">
    <ComboboxPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Combobox usage"
      code={`import {
  Combobox,
  ComboboxContent,
  ComboboxEmpty,
  ComboboxInput,
  ComboboxItem,
  ComboboxList,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/combobox";

const fruits = ["Apple", "Apricot", "Blueberry", "Cherry", "Pear"];

<Combobox items={fruits}>
  <ComboboxInput aria-label="Choose a fruit" placeholder="Choose a fruit" showClear />
  <ComboboxContent>
    <ComboboxEmpty>No fruit found.</ComboboxEmpty>
    <ComboboxList>
      {(item) => (
        <ComboboxItem key={item} value={item}>
          {item}
        </ComboboxItem>
      )}
    </ComboboxList>
  </ComboboxContent>
</Combobox>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>items</code> to <code>Combobox</code> and a function to <code>ComboboxList</code>. The list filters as
      you type, and <code>ComboboxEmpty</code> shows when nothing matches. For objects, pass{' '}
      <code>itemToStringLabel</code> and
      <code>isItemEqualToValue</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Single, multiple, and disabled</h2>
    <p>
      These are the three forms TulipFarm uses: a single choice with a clear button, many choices as chips with a
      starting value, and a disabled field.
    </p>
    <ComboboxBasics client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Input options</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ComboboxInput</code> shows a chevron by default. Turn it off with <code>showTrigger={'{false}'}</code> so
      the list opens on typing or ↓. <code>showClear</code> adds a clear button that replaces the chevron once there is
      a value. Children are added to the group, such as a leading icon.
    </p>
    <ComboboxInputOptions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Chips</h2>
    <p>
      With <code>multiple</code>, render <code>ComboboxChip</code>s from <code>ComboboxValue</code> inside{' '}
      <code>ComboboxChips</code>, then a <code>ComboboxChipsInput</code>. Pass a ref from <code>useComboboxAnchor</code>{' '}
      to the chips and to <code>ComboboxContent</code>’s <code>anchor</code> so the list matches the field. Set{' '}
      <code>showRemove={'{false}'}</code> on a chip that must stay. Chips wrap when they don’t fit.
    </p>
    <ComboboxMultiple client:load />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Chips"
      code={`const anchor = useComboboxAnchor();

<Combobox items={channels} multiple defaultValue={["launches"]}>
  <ComboboxChips ref={anchor}>
    <ComboboxValue>
      {(values: string[]) =>
        values.map((value) => <ComboboxChip key={value}>{value}</ComboboxChip>)
      }
    </ComboboxValue>
    <ComboboxChipsInput aria-label="Alert channels" placeholder="Add channel" />
  </ComboboxChips>
  <ComboboxContent anchor={anchor}>
    <ComboboxEmpty>No channel found.</ComboboxEmpty>
    <ComboboxList>
      {(channel) => <ComboboxItem key={channel} value={channel}>{channel}</ComboboxItem>}
    </ComboboxList>
  </ComboboxContent>
</Combobox>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Trigger button</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ComboboxTrigger</code> can be the whole control. Render it as a <code>Button</code>, show{' '}
      <code>ComboboxValue</code> inside, and put a <code>ComboboxInput</code> with <code>showTrigger={'{false}'}</code>{' '}
      at the top of the list. With no children it is an icon button named “Show options”.
    </p>
    <ComboboxTriggerPicker client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Groups and separators</h2>
    <p>
      Pass groups as <code>items</code>. Render each one as a <code>ComboboxGroup</code> with its own <code>items</code>
      , a <code>ComboboxLabel</code>, and a<code>ComboboxCollection</code>. Put a <code>ComboboxSeparator</code>
      between groups.
    </p>
    <ComboboxGroups client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      While items load, pass an empty list, set <code>aria-busy</code> on the input, and say so in{' '}
      <code>ComboboxEmpty</code>. Set <code>aria-invalid</code> and point <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error.
      Disabled items can be reached with the arrow keys but can’t be chosen. A disabled combobox can’t be focused.
    </p>
    <ComboboxStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="combobox-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Combobox</code> is the Base UI combobox root. It takes <code>items</code>, <code>multiple</code>,{' '}
      <code>value</code>, <code>defaultValue</code>,<code>onValueChange</code>, <code>itemToStringLabel</code>,{' '}
      <code>disabled</code>, <code>name</code>, and every other root prop.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ComboboxInput</code> takes <code>showTrigger</code> (true), <code>showClear</code> (false),{' '}
      <code>disabled</code>, and every input prop. Its <code>className</code> goes on the <code>InputGroup</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ComboboxContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It takes
      <code>side</code> (bottom), <code>align</code> (start), <code>sideOffset</code> (6), <code>alignOffset</code> (0),
      and <code>anchor</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ComboboxChip</code> takes <code>showRemove</code> (true). <code>ComboboxTrigger</code>,{' '}
      <code>ComboboxValue</code>, <code>ComboboxList</code>, <code>ComboboxItem</code>, <code>ComboboxGroup</code>,{' '}
      <code>ComboboxLabel</code>, <code>ComboboxCollection</code>, <code>ComboboxEmpty</code>,{' '}
      <code>ComboboxSeparator</code>, <code>ComboboxChips</code>, and <code>ComboboxChipsInput</code> wrap the Base UI
      parts and take their props. <code>useComboboxAnchor</code> returns a ref for the chips. Every part sets a{' '}
      <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The input is a combobox with <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-autocomplete</code>. Typing or ↓ opens the
      list. Arrow keys move, Enter picks, and Escape closes and keeps focus in the input. In a chips field, ← and → move
      between chips and Backspace removes one. Each remove button is named “Remove” plus the chip text.{' '}
      <code>ComboboxEmpty</code> is a polite live region.
    </p>
    <p>
      The list fades and scales in over 120ms. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested. On touch screens items
      are at least 44px tall. In forced-colors mode the highlighted item gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Comboboxes use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-canvas</code>, <code>--sprout-input</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code>--sprout-secondary</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code>--sprout-danger</code>
      , <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the control and panel radii. Only the focus ring follows the brand, so
      they work with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
